  "result": "I opened the issue: https://github.com/acme/textstats/issues/13. I didn't change any code.\n\n- **Title:** \"word_count returns 1 for an empty string (expected 0)\".\n- **Reproduction:** `word_count(\"\")` returns 1, and it should return 0.\n- **Cause:** `textstats/__init__.py`, lines 4-6, does `len(text.split(\" \"))`. `\"\".split(\" \")` returns `[\"\"]`, which has length 1.\n- **Related problem:** Splitting on a single space also miscounts repeated or leading/trailing spaces. For example, `\"a  b\"` gives 3. `average_word_length` in the same file uses `text.split()`, which handles those cases.\n- **Acceptance criteria:** `word_count(\"\")` returns 0, and a regression test is added in `tests/test_textstats.py`.",
